 "detailedDescription": "This is a Phase 2/3 Adaptive Design, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of DM199 for the Treatment of Acute Ischemic Stroke (ReMEDy2 Trial). Participants with AIS will be randomized 1:1 to DM199 or placebo. DM199 will be administered as a single intravenous (IV) dose (0.5 μg/kg; not to exceed 50 μg) followed by subcutaneous (SC) doses at 2 hours (+10 hours) of the IV dose completion and then 2 times per week up to Day 21. The duration of each individual's participation in the study will be approximately 90 days from the time of initial treatment to completion of all study activities.\n\nA formal interim analysis will be conducted after 200 participants complete their Day 90 assessment in Part A. The purposes of this interim analysis are to assess safety, allow early stopping of the study for futility, or continuing the study with a revised final sample up to a maximum of 728 participants.",
