 "enrollment": 336,
 "briefSummary": "This will be a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multi-centre study with the aim to establish metabolic improvements in individuals diagnosed with hyperuricemia associated with gout by treatment with CMA2 including N-acetyl-L-cysteine (NAC), L-carnitine-L-tartrate (LCAT), nicotinamide (niacinamide), and L-serine for 4 weeks.",
 "detailedDescription": "Consenting participants will be screened for eligibility (Visit 1; screening) according to study-specific eligibility criteria within 7 days prior to randomisation and start of investigational medicinal product (IMP) administration.\n\nEligible participants will be randomised on Day 1 (Visit 2) to 4 weeks of twice daily (b.i.d.) oral treatment of either CMA2 or placebo (1:1). The first dose will be administered at the study clinic. The participants will be observed for 2 hours post dose for the development of any allergic reactions or intolerance after taking the first dose.\n\nVisits at the study site will be performed at Day 1 (Visit 2), Day 14 (Visit 4) and Day 28 (Visit 6; end of in study treatment). There will be telephone follow up visits at Day 7 (Visit 3) and Day 21(Visit 5) checking safety, concomitant medications and IMP compliance. A final follow-up visit for safety assessments will be conducted in a subgroup of patients 14 days after the end of treatment (Day 42; Visit 7) during an IMP-free follow-up period to assess safety and concomitant medications.\n\nThe following clinical scales will be used to evaluate the effect of CMA2 on uric acid decline, hsCRP and daily life activity: Serum Uric Acid Levels, hsCRP, number of flares according to the GAFFO criteria, HAQ-DI, SF-36, PGA (100 mm).\n\nPlasma samples will be collected for advanced metabolomics, proteomics, and lipidomics analysis.\n\nOptionally, synovial samples will be collected for advanced metabolomics, proteomics, and lipidomics analysis. Optionally, gut and saliva samples will be collected for metagenomics analysis of gut and oral microbiome.\n\nLaboratory and clinical safety parameters will be monitored at pre-specified time-points.",
 "arms": [
  {
